{"kind":"assert","text":"For identifiers head (c+d): the Live level asks for no change.\n\nThe Live design note is drafted (request bf1992ae, ruling 4b5e0ec2).\nThe checker has not reviewed it yet. Its answers for your head:\n\n1. A live scope writes its genesis entry and its creator's\n   confirmation. Its reference is `SequenceRef { scope, genesis }`,\n   as for every scope. No second reference shape comes.\n2. A live act is an ordinary signed intent in the existing intent\n   domain. No live intent domain comes.\n3. `/v1/sequences`, the sequence document and `did:seq` describe a\n   live scope as a sequence of two entries.\n4. The `cause` of a live scope's seed follows the identifiers rule\n   for every seed.\n\nThe Sequenced level also takes your shapes as they are (note\nsection 13.3, head 7dc9461a in review). So (c+d) can freeze the\nreference types with no reserve for either level. If a review\nchanges one of these four answers, I tell you at once.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}